1
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,190
You got the answer,

2
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:11,820
so you deserve the prize.

3
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,760
I don't need money.

4
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:17,530
Once I am old enough to use that money,

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,260
its monetary value would have dropped.

6
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,240
Is that so?

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,200
I'd like land.

8
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:29,070
A place with lots of plants and trees.

9
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:37,420
I like this area, right here.

10
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:43,920
That land was used to make pottery. It's useless.

11
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:44,920
(Gyeonggi Province, Seongnam, Bundang-dong)

12
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:46,930
Do you want the land in Bundang that badly?

13
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,730
Let's see.

14
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:55,770
How does 160,000m² sound?

15
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:57,540
(Gyeonggi Province, Seongnam, Bundang-dong)

16
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:01,210
This small village will become a new city,

17
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:02,810
home to 390,000 people.

18
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:05,640
According to the government's New Town development plan,

19
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:07,450
on Seongnam's Bundang area,

20
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:10,280
about 105,000 medium to large apartment blocks will be built.

21
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:13,220
They will reduce the burden on Gangnam's housing demand...

22
00:01:13,390 --> 00:01:15,690
by housing 420,000 people.

23
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:18,960
What an incredible change this place went through.

24
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,460
There was just one reservoir...

25
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:27,000
with fields and rice paddies reaching the horizons.

26
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:30,070
People say that Bundang...

27
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,800
is the next best place to live, second to paradise.

28
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,310
Did you know then...

29
00:01:40,010 --> 00:01:41,650
that this place would become like this?

30
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,720
Do you simply have good discernment?

31
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,890
Or are you just lucky?

32
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:56,130
I owe it to a grandfather who gifted me 160,000m² of land.

33
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:00,000
Not anyone gets to be born your grandson.

34
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,300
Does that make me lucky?

35
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,270
From the land here,

36
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,770
do you know how much you made?

37
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,080
Welcome, sir.

38
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:20,020
This way, please.

39
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:28,560
The 24 million dollars you asked for.

40
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:30,330
Good.

41
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:41,040
The compensation for the purchase of land was 14 million.

42
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:44,940
Ten million was from selling the nearby commercial land.

43
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:48,080
A total of 24 million dollars...

44
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:51,120
is what you earned.

45
00:02:55,450 --> 00:02:57,090
Would you like to count it out?

46
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:15,610
How will you manage to spend all this?

47
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,740
If you buy books with it,

48
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,050
you'll never read them all in your lifetime.

49
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:22,850
If you spend it on tuition,

50
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:26,050
you'll have to get a hundred degrees.

51
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:29,050
If you're afraid, leave it with me.

52
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,260
I'll pay you more in interest than a bank does.

53
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:43,600
(Reborn Rich)

54
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:50,040
Do Jun is still a kid, isn't he?

55
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,710
It's only natural.

56
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:55,250
Where could he have seen such a huge amount?

57
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:59,520
Sir, Hangang Bank's Namdaemun Branch called.

58
00:04:00,890 --> 00:04:04,290
Do Jun has exchanged the money in the account into dollars.

59
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:10,700
Shouldn't you ask him what it's for?

60
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:15,630
He may be clever,

61
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,870
but it's too much money for a 20-year-old.

62
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:23,780
Does money choose people depending on their age?

63
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:29,380
Let's find out if Do Jun...

64
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:32,020
is a fortunate boy,

65
00:04:32,550 --> 00:04:34,290
or a boy with foresight.

66
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:37,190
It's just luck.

67
00:04:37,990 --> 00:04:40,160
How else can you explain it?

68
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:43,530
What could a little boy know about real estate...

69
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:45,230
that he'd ask for land in Bundang?

70
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:50,600
No one can beat someone with great luck.

71
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,770
Doesn't that make him even scarier?

72
00:04:53,970 --> 00:04:56,370
What does Father say almost every day?

73
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:59,380
You don't become rich by working hard.

74
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,710
It's up to the heavens.

75
00:05:01,650 --> 00:05:03,980
Do Jun made 24 million dollars...

76
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:05,820
by just pointing at a map.

77
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:08,490
Father could think...

78
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:11,490
his youngest grandson is blessed.

79
00:05:11,490 --> 00:05:12,520
Wait.

80
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:18,500
Is that why? Isn't it weird?

81
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:22,070
Dad gave that massive sum to a kid who just started college...

82
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:23,400
and let him manage it himself.

83
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,840
He's not that kind of person.

84
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:29,270
He never let us do anything like that.

85
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:33,180
Not even Seong Jun, his eldest grandson.

86
00:05:36,350 --> 00:05:37,350
Right?

87
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:45,690
Seong Jun is the eldest heir,

88
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:48,390
and he was exiled in the name of study.

89
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:51,560
Why does Father play favourites with the youngest, Do Jun?

90
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,660
That money.

91
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:56,570
It's the price of our father's life.

92
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:00,640
If not for Do Jun,

93
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:04,040
when the plane exploded in mid air,

94
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:07,210
Father would've died in it.

95
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:13,490
Who cares if it's 24 million or 240 million?

96
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:15,550
It's too early for such a fuss.

97
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:22,930
Don't you feel ashamed?

98
00:06:23,230 --> 00:06:26,500
You're jealous about a 20-year-old boy's allowance.

99
00:06:29,270 --> 00:06:31,240
You're grown-up adults.

100
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:34,270
Do you really think so?

101
00:06:36,610 --> 00:06:37,880
That it's allowance?

102
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:40,280
That it's a simple gift?

103
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,450
It could be a test.

104
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:52,560
Father could be testing the boy with plans on picking a successor.

105
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:07,870
What is it that I am

106
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:13,010
Trying to look for?

107
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:18,220
Where to is it that I am

108
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:22,890
Flowing so endlessly?

109
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:26,790
The upcoming New York Film Market.

110
00:07:28,130 --> 00:07:29,660
Take me with you, Father.

111
00:07:30,030 --> 00:07:31,200
To the Film Market?

112
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,530
I got into university,

113
00:07:33,530 --> 00:07:35,930
but I have lots of time until the semester starts.

114
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:37,740
I'd like to travel,

115
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:41,710
and maybe do some advising on what films you should invest in.

116
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:43,910
You'll be an investment advisor?

117
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,610
You know I have a good eye.

118
00:07:47,610 --> 00:07:50,650
I think I'm the one who got you this office.

119
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:56,120
I must release this movie on Christmas at all costs?

120
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,160
Do Jun.

121
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,130
You're still young and don't know about movies.

122
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:07,830
Christmas movies are for families.

123
00:08:08,170 --> 00:08:10,970
Who'd want to watch a gloomy movie about a kid...

124
00:08:10,970 --> 00:08:13,540
left alone at home while his family went travelling?

125
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:16,770
And you still...

126
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,440
want me to import this movie?

127
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:29,090
So you want to go to the New York Film Market?

128
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:32,690
Yes. Who knows?

129
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:36,090
This time, it might not be just an office.

130
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,200
Perhaps I could buy you a whole building.

131
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:42,230
There was no me anymore

132
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:46,970
We are still young We still have a nice future

133
00:08:46,970 --> 00:08:49,640
Now wipe up your cold tears

134
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,440
Come back home

135
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,780
Let's go home now.

136
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:55,850
- You go ahead. - Come with me.

137
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:58,220
I'm not Seo Tai Ji.

138
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,890
Oh, gosh...

139
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,520
- Hey, Do Jun. - What?

140
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:05,060
Just because you got into law top of the class,

141
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:06,660
don't get fancy and have dreams...

142
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,760
of passing the bar while you're still in college.

143
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:10,900
What?

144
00:09:11,230 --> 00:09:12,860
Play. Have fun.

145
00:09:13,230 --> 00:09:16,870
Go on group blind dates, regular blind dates, casual dates,

146
00:09:16,870 --> 00:09:18,200
- and go out with someone. - Hang on.

147
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:20,040
Are they all different?

148
00:09:21,010 --> 00:09:24,080
Are they the same, then? They have different terms.

149
00:09:25,310 --> 00:09:26,810
Don't do that.

150
00:09:27,250 --> 00:09:30,580
Don't make the face of a man who already lived a lifetime.

151
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,250
- What? - Don't do that either.

152
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:33,650
- I'll do it. - Go away.

153
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:35,290
Wait, what's that?

154
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:38,690
- No way. - What do we do now?

155
00:09:39,390 --> 00:09:40,890
What is it?

156
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:42,060
Excuse me.

157
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:44,260
- They'd caused a fuss... - Excuse me.

158
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,600
- Coming through. - Sorry.

159
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:49,330
- They announced their retirement. - What is it?

160
00:09:49,470 --> 00:09:53,000
As of today, January 31, 1996...

161
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,310
Are they disbanding or retiring?

162
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:57,410
They're retiring.

163
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:07,020
- Oh, no... - Jeez.

164
00:10:07,050 --> 00:10:08,950
(Seo Min Yeong)

165
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:11,920
Why are they retiring?

166
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:13,160
My loves.

167
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:17,160
They're retiring because the pain of creating music is too much.

168
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:21,600
(Seo Min Yeong)

169
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:50,900
What's this?

170
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,170
This is a look I've never seen on your face.

171
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:57,200
I can't believe that's her face when she was 20.

172
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,300
Do you know her?

173
00:11:00,810 --> 00:11:02,410
Did you meet her? When?

174
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,040
What?

175
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,480
Oh...

176
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:09,950
In 20 years' time.

177
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:15,020
"In 20 years' time."

178
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:16,890
He's at it again.

179
00:11:16,890 --> 00:11:18,290
Move, mister.

180
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:19,960
- Move. - Okay.

181
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,330
- I can't see. - I'm not a mister.

182
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:29,370
Chang Je, are you getting old?

183
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,940
You shouldn't be up this early. What's going on?

184
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,870
Why are you coming to see me?

185
00:11:36,610 --> 00:11:38,440
Take a look at this, Father.

186
00:11:39,710 --> 00:11:40,950
(Seoul District Public Prosecutors' Office)

187
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:49,120
(Report on Special Investigation into Hando Steel)

188
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:52,390
I don't think Hando Steel will last a month.

189
00:11:52,590 --> 00:11:54,790
It's a great chance to buy it up cheap.

190
00:11:54,790 --> 00:11:57,160
They took out too many loans to try to expand.

191
00:11:57,830 --> 00:11:59,960
If you underwrite Hando Steel now,

192
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:02,970
wouldn't it help subsidiaries that use steel...

193
00:12:02,970 --> 00:12:06,770
such as Soonyang Heavy Machinery, Motors, and Machinery?

194
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:11,540
How will they handle this much debt?

195
00:12:12,410 --> 00:12:14,610
If the government vouches for us,

196
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:17,520
we can extend the repayment deadline to suit us.

197
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:21,790
Can we trust President YS?

198
00:12:21,990 --> 00:12:24,420
If Hando Group were to break up now,

199
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:26,390
it would cause huge turmoil.

200
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:28,830
The President would want to prevent the worst.

201
00:12:31,630 --> 00:12:33,460
Having a prosecutor son-in-law...

202
00:12:34,370 --> 00:12:35,700
is so reassuring.

203
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:38,170
I thought I should give you...

204
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,070
one last gift while I still work there.

205
00:12:41,370 --> 00:12:42,370
What?

206
00:12:42,870 --> 00:12:45,080
Are you going to start a law firm?

207
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,550
Before the general election in April,

208
00:12:48,550 --> 00:12:51,050
the President will recruit talent to join his party.

209
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:55,420
I'd love to join as a legal advisor and run for office.

210
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:56,690
The National Assembly is on an island.

211
00:12:57,220 --> 00:13:00,690
It'll be very windy out there. Do you want to get into politics?

212
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,660
You can give me a sail.

213
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:06,560
I want to venture into bigger waters for Soonyang.

214
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,370
I'll see...

215
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:18,380
if my son-in-law's ship can survive the sea.

216
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:22,910
I'll do my best not to let you down, Father.

217
00:13:48,910 --> 00:13:51,440
Something that dreamy would never happen.

218
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:57,080
One day, will a Korean movie ever beat Hollywood movies...

219
00:13:57,180 --> 00:14:00,180
to win Best Picture at the Academy Awards?

220
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:04,360
That's something out of a sci-Fi cartoon that makes me emotional.

221
00:14:05,990 --> 00:14:07,390
It won't be easy.

222
00:14:07,690 --> 00:14:11,260
The Academy Awards tend to snuff non-English movies.

223
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,670
I'm too imaginative.

224
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,330
If that day comes,

225
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:18,740
a Korean song might even reach Billboard's Top 100.

226
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:22,910
I know.

227
00:14:22,910 --> 00:14:24,640
What I'm saying is as likely as Team Korea...

228
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,640
reaching the semifinals of the FIFA World Cup.

229
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:29,280
Can't a man dream?

230
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:30,820
Don't you know dreams come true?

231
00:14:31,650 --> 00:14:34,150
Darn you. Wait up, Dad.

232
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:39,060
Yes.

233
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:41,290
Dreams do come true.

234
00:14:47,570 --> 00:14:49,670
- Oh. - I'm sorry.

235
00:14:49,670 --> 00:14:52,770
What the... This is just not fair.

236
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:55,340
Darn it.

237
00:14:56,670 --> 00:14:58,540
Are you Korean?

238
00:15:02,250 --> 00:15:03,280
Shoot.

239
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,590
If you mean nationality, no.

240
00:15:10,590 --> 00:15:12,690
If you mean where I was born, yes.

241
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:15,090
We're halfway around the world.

242
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:17,600
You're not expecting a friendly hug, are you?

243
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,400
Look.

244
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:23,170
Because of you, I just became the investor...

245
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:26,840
with the most rotten luck in the whole of this market.

246
00:15:27,370 --> 00:15:28,870
Oh, then...

247
00:15:30,070 --> 00:15:31,710
I'm truly sorry.

248
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:33,840
I'll pay you for the donut.

249
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:37,050
- How much do you want? - Ten million dollars!

250
00:15:39,450 --> 00:15:40,550
Ten million dollars?

251
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:44,320
What are you talking about?

252
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:46,490
One donut costs ten million dollars?

253
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:50,160
I always eat a donut before I decide what to invest in.

254
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:52,100
I've never broken it once.

255
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:54,170
It's a principle, routine, and jinx. Anyway,

256
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:55,800
it's my most important, necessary,

257
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,470
and sufficient condition of investing.

258
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:01,370
This donut is from a shop in Midtown that's 30 minutes from here.

259
00:16:01,470 --> 00:16:05,040
And I have just ten minutes to decide what to invest in.

260
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,910
Without a donut,

261
00:16:07,010 --> 00:16:10,310
in this market where ten million dollars will change hands,

262
00:16:10,410 --> 00:16:11,850
because of clumsy you.

263
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:14,420
You'll pay me back?

264
00:16:15,190 --> 00:16:18,720
This donut cost a dollar, but it's worth ten million to me.

265
00:16:19,290 --> 00:16:20,620
How much will you pay me?

266
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:26,200
Never bet on things...

267
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,930
that you aren't sure about.

268
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:31,500
Do you get that?

269
00:16:35,010 --> 00:16:36,040
That...

270
00:16:47,050 --> 00:16:48,820
Do Jun! We're over here.

271
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:50,450
Okay. I'm coming.

272
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:54,730
What a weirdo.

273
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,040
"Titanic."

274
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:08,170
The "Titanic" fever is going strong.

275
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:13,040
Nominated for 14 Academy Awards, the most in Academy history,

276
00:17:13,210 --> 00:17:15,510
at the 70th Academy Awards...

277
00:17:15,510 --> 00:17:17,280
I should invest in "Titanic?"

278
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,550
Yes.

279
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:21,290
Not for import or distribution rights...

280
00:17:21,690 --> 00:17:23,290
but the production?

281
00:17:23,890 --> 00:17:24,890
Yes.

282
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:29,060
That way, you get a part of the massive profit.

283
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:30,690
It goes here.

284
00:17:30,690 --> 00:17:32,230
There are three arches.

285
00:17:32,230 --> 00:17:33,330
- Shall we bet? - Yes.

286
00:17:33,330 --> 00:17:37,000
Do Jun. The reason you wanted to come here...

287
00:17:37,270 --> 00:17:39,800
was because you had this movie in mind from the start?

288
00:17:45,610 --> 00:17:47,340
Hey. Look, Father.

289
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:49,850
My gosh.

290
00:17:51,250 --> 00:17:53,250
Wow. Nice.

291
00:17:56,590 --> 00:17:59,520
Are you convinced it will be a hit?

292
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,960
Like "Home Alone" last time?

293
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:08,030
You know I have a good hunch.

294
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,400
Trust me again.

295
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:13,540
A hunch?

296
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,410
Father. I have a scientific...

297
00:18:19,410 --> 00:18:22,150
and logical reason this movie will flop.

298
00:18:22,150 --> 00:18:23,410
It'll shock you.

299
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:27,890
Blockbusters involving water...

300
00:18:28,490 --> 00:18:31,190
are bound to flop.

301
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:32,260
Why?

302
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,960
Because the project sinks.

303
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:39,760
What?

304
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:42,530
"Cut throat Island," "Waterworld,"

305
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:47,470
and serial hit-maker James Cameron's only flop "The Abyss."

306
00:18:47,470 --> 00:18:50,210
They're all about water, and they all tanked.

307
00:18:50,210 --> 00:18:52,840
This is a science.

308
00:18:53,010 --> 00:18:55,110
Boss, you need to think this over.

309
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:56,580
You have to think this over.

310
00:18:56,710 --> 00:18:58,420
You would've never made this decision...

311
00:18:58,420 --> 00:19:00,120
if you didn't drop that darn donut.

312
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:03,390
Ten million dollars into "Titanic?"

313
00:19:03,990 --> 00:19:05,860
Why don't you take that ten million dollars...

314
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,990
and just throw it into the Atlantic Ocean?

315
00:19:07,990 --> 00:19:10,190
Will you still invest in "Titanic?"

316
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:14,030
Come on. You didn't even watch "Waterworld."

317
00:19:14,030 --> 00:19:15,070
I couldn't.

318
00:19:15,170 --> 00:19:16,230
DiCaprio?

319
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,140
DiCaprio?

320
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,240
Who on earth will do the acting?

321
00:19:20,370 --> 00:19:22,970
And the woman who looks like his aunt.

322
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:24,710
Do Koreans even know who she is?

323
00:19:25,110 --> 00:19:27,010
Do you know her? I don't know her.

324
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,950
- No Brad Pitt or Tom Cruise. - They're Korean.

325
00:19:30,050 --> 00:19:32,180
A blockbuster with zero stars?

326
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:34,890
Do you really think this will work, boss?

327
00:19:35,650 --> 00:19:36,720
"Titanic."

328
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:39,560
It's about a luxury cruise ship that's only for the rich...

329
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:42,390
sinking in a gruesome manner in the middle of nowhere.

330
00:19:42,390 --> 00:19:44,030
It's about the rich losing out.

331
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:46,030
People have no choice but to flock to the cinemas.

332
00:19:46,030 --> 00:19:48,070
Why? Because it'll never happen in reality.

333
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:49,900
Did you hear that?

334
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:52,800
She looks like DiCaprio's aunt?

335
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:57,070
She's the real reason I want to invest in this movie.

336
00:19:57,310 --> 00:19:58,340
What?

337
00:19:58,340 --> 00:19:59,880
In a recession like this,

338
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:02,710
the public care very little for cute, young starlets.

339
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:05,220
They prefer mature actresses with an intellectual air...

340
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:06,780
to be their heroine.

341
00:20:06,950 --> 00:20:09,350
Kate Winslet has that face.

342
00:20:09,350 --> 00:20:11,690
They spent an enormous amount of money to make the movie.

343
00:20:11,890 --> 00:20:15,060
It won't be profitable unless it becomes an international hit.

344
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:17,030
Following Europe,

345
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:19,030
countries in East Asia are building multiplex theatres too.

346
00:20:19,030 --> 00:20:21,500
The number of movie goers will increase exponentially.

347
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:23,730
And naturally, the profitability will go up as well.

348
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:26,570
You know what a low-price high-volume policy means, right?

349
00:20:27,970 --> 00:20:29,270
Are you confident?

350
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:31,840
Can I guarantee that the movie will be a hit?

351
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:33,810
Then my answer is no. However,

352
00:20:34,510 --> 00:20:35,880
if it's about recovering the investment...

353
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:39,050
and securing stable profitability... Yes.

354
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:43,050
- He's right. - I'm very rational now, Rachael.

355
00:20:43,950 --> 00:20:46,990
I said I dropped the donut.

356
00:20:48,090 --> 00:20:49,930
I never said I didn't eat it.

357
00:20:50,190 --> 00:20:51,230
What?

358
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:58,600
"Based on scientific evidence..."

359
00:21:00,270 --> 00:21:01,840
is what I'd say in a situation like this.

360
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:04,110
- Hey! - How's it going?

361
00:21:04,110 --> 00:21:05,480
- I'm good. - Yes.

362
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,840
Are you going to invest in this?

363
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:08,780
- That's what I'm thinking about. - What about you?

364
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:10,280
- I'm investing... - Do you have anything in mind?

365
00:21:10,280 --> 00:21:12,120
- Power Shares? - Yes, I have...

366
00:21:23,090 --> 00:21:24,600
Mason Oh.

367
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:28,300
His Korean name is Oh Se Hyeon.

368
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,500
Power Shares.

369
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,970
The director and head of APAC at Power Shares.

370
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:46,980
Hi, good afternoon.

371
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:48,350
Hi, may I help you?

372
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:50,420
Yes. I'm Jin.

373
00:21:50,890 --> 00:21:53,020
I'm here to see Mason Oh.

374
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:57,830
- I got twenty on Kasparov. - Fifty on Kasparov.

375
00:21:57,830 --> 00:21:59,430
We're nuts for doing this.

376
00:21:59,430 --> 00:22:01,830
I want to put... If you guys let me get in on...

377
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:06,670
I'm surprised to see you here. I thought...

378
00:22:06,670 --> 00:22:08,810
you'd been in a business meeting somewhere.

379
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:15,450
Thanks to you,

380
00:22:15,850 --> 00:22:19,550
I became the luckiest investor on Wall Street today.

381
00:22:19,950 --> 00:22:22,120
Here's your delicious cheese pizza.

382
00:22:23,450 --> 00:22:24,790
Enjoy your meal.

383
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,220
- Thank you. - Thank you.

384
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:40,640
What's that guy doing?

385
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:42,770
Is he crazy or something?

386
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,180
Maybe you should order something else.

387
00:22:50,350 --> 00:22:52,980
Darn it. This is so good.

388
00:22:53,850 --> 00:22:56,350
This is the best cheese I've ever had.

389
00:22:57,290 --> 00:22:59,890
I should've bought some shares in this cheese company back then.

390
00:23:00,690 --> 00:23:01,930
It's too late now.

391
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:04,960
Darn, it's so good.

392
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:09,500
Hey, you. I wanted to say something earlier.

393
00:23:09,900 --> 00:23:12,940
I am working right now.

394
00:23:13,570 --> 00:23:16,370
Leave me alone, will you? Don't disturb me.

395
00:23:20,210 --> 00:23:22,010
Well, that's the right move, by the way.

396
00:23:22,010 --> 00:23:24,310
- Oh. - Yes, that is the right move.

397
00:23:24,310 --> 00:23:26,380
That was absolutely amazing.

398
00:23:27,850 --> 00:23:29,590
The supercomputer Deep Blue...

399
00:23:30,290 --> 00:23:33,520
versus Kasparov, the chess champion.

400
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:37,490
What a strange world we live in.

401
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:40,460
Even a computer has a name?

402
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:42,870
Hyeon Woo, what was it called?

403
00:23:42,870 --> 00:23:45,840
You know, that computer. Blue... What was it?

404
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:47,740
Dad!

405
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:50,410
- Dad! - What is it, son?

406
00:23:51,070 --> 00:23:52,480
- Wow. - Why? Who won?

407
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:54,610
My gosh. Unbelievable.

408
00:23:58,320 --> 00:23:59,820
Who do you think will win?

409
00:24:01,650 --> 00:24:03,950
The supercomputer Deep Blue?

410
00:24:04,690 --> 00:24:07,890
Or Garry Kasparov, the chess champion?

411
00:24:08,660 --> 00:24:09,660
Who?

412
00:24:11,630 --> 00:24:12,630
Well...

413
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,630
Everyone says it's the game of the century...

414
00:24:14,630 --> 00:24:16,200
between a human and a computer.

415
00:24:16,370 --> 00:24:18,300
But that's not what you're interested in, right?

416
00:24:20,940 --> 00:24:24,370
"What is the company value of IBM, the company that made Deep Blue?"

417
00:24:24,370 --> 00:24:27,010
"When and how much should I buy in to maximize my profit?"

418
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:30,710
That's why you're so engrossed in the match. Am I right?

419
00:24:33,250 --> 00:24:34,950
I'll tell you who will win.

420
00:24:34,950 --> 00:24:38,690
In turn, spare me your time.

421
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:42,430
You can tell me who will win when the match is still going on?

422
00:24:46,630 --> 00:24:48,030
Deep Blue will win.

423
00:24:48,770 --> 00:24:51,200
Invest in IBM, before this round ends.

424
00:24:54,710 --> 00:24:55,770
Can I have a piece?

425
00:24:59,610 --> 00:25:04,050
Well, chances are... It's 50-50 anyway.

426
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:07,520
I guess you're relying on luck. Too bad.

427
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:10,820
Deep Blue hasn't overcome the limitations of AI.

428
00:25:10,820 --> 00:25:13,260
Even the engineers and developers at IBM admitted it.

429
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:17,860
But you think Deep Blue will beat Kasparov, the genius player?

430
00:25:19,300 --> 00:25:22,030
Deep Blue has less than a 20-percent chance to win.

431
00:25:22,930 --> 00:25:25,570
That's what all experts say. Hey, young man.

432
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:30,440
Never bet on things that you aren't sure about.

433
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:33,540
I never rely on luck when it comes to my investments.

434
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:49,660
When the game ends,

435
00:25:50,860 --> 00:25:54,530
you'll want to meet me.

436
00:25:58,300 --> 00:25:59,500
I'm confident.

437
00:26:00,670 --> 00:26:03,240
I'm 100 percent sure that Deep Blue will win.

438
00:26:03,410 --> 00:26:04,640
Hey, go away.

439
00:26:16,220 --> 00:26:17,590
Oh, my gosh!

440
00:26:18,460 --> 00:26:19,960
- No problem! - Yes!

441
00:26:20,790 --> 00:26:23,760
- I can't believe it. - Thank you, gentlemen. Sorry, man.

442
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:25,330
What? Deep Blue won?

443
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:29,530
A supercomputer beat a human for the first time in history?

444
00:26:57,060 --> 00:26:58,500
That was a fluke, right?

445
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:06,940
How did you guess it?

446
00:27:08,010 --> 00:27:10,570
None of the experts on Wall Street...

447
00:27:10,570 --> 00:27:13,710
predicted that Deep Blue would win.

448
00:27:19,320 --> 00:27:20,380
I trusted my instincts.

449
00:27:21,420 --> 00:27:22,420
What?

450
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:24,760
Had Kasparov been a mere player,

451
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:27,620
Deep Blue wouldn't have stood a chance against him.

452
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:31,360
However, I bet Kasparov, the genius chess player...

453
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:33,530
who's kept the world champion title for the past 20 years,

454
00:27:34,900 --> 00:27:36,500
wanted to make history.

455
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:40,100
"Fought against AI and won,"

456
00:27:40,100 --> 00:27:42,210
"thus protecting the pride of mankind."

457
00:27:43,070 --> 00:27:44,680
He probably wanted a title like that.

458
00:27:45,340 --> 00:27:48,610
And greed...

459
00:27:49,110 --> 00:27:51,450
always clouds your judgement.

460
00:27:54,380 --> 00:27:55,590
Not bad.

461
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:02,030
I'd like to invest in companies in the US.

462
00:28:03,860 --> 00:28:07,360
Relying on your instincts, knowing how risky that can be?

463
00:28:08,470 --> 00:28:09,900
I have you.

464
00:28:10,570 --> 00:28:13,770
Use numbers to help me prove that my instincts are on point.

465
00:28:15,040 --> 00:28:16,770
I'm a busy man, you see.

466
00:28:18,140 --> 00:28:19,580
Enjoy the rest of your trip.

467
00:28:21,380 --> 00:28:23,580
With accurate data, which is essential for investing.

468
00:28:24,150 --> 00:28:28,150
And with cash.

469
00:28:29,690 --> 00:28:31,720
Do you know that the minimum amount we require...

470
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:34,320
is 30,000 dollars?

471
00:28:35,430 --> 00:28:36,860
I have a lot of money, Mr. Oh.

472
00:28:37,190 --> 00:28:40,460
Save up as much as you can before you join the military.

473
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,270
Enjoy your trip. Bye.

474
00:28:49,010 --> 00:28:51,370
(Jeongsimjae)

475
00:28:57,050 --> 00:28:58,850
As for Hando Steel, we're estimating...

476
00:28:58,850 --> 00:29:00,420
that it'd cost us about 500 million dollars.

477
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:04,220
So we'll go penniless after this deal.

478
00:29:05,260 --> 00:29:07,090
Do they have something we could use to make money?

479
00:29:07,090 --> 00:29:10,060
Hando Steel owns a warehouse in Busan.

480
00:29:10,160 --> 00:29:12,060
If we make sure the creditors can't touch it...

481
00:29:12,130 --> 00:29:13,900
and build an apartment complex in that lot,

482
00:29:14,630 --> 00:29:17,100
we should be able to earn back the money fairly soon.

483
00:29:17,930 --> 00:29:20,570
Sir, we've encountered an unexpected variable though.

484
00:29:21,270 --> 00:29:24,540
Daeyoung Group is getting ready to bid on Hando Steel too.

485
00:29:24,910 --> 00:29:27,740
The Secretary's Office informed me this morning.

486
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:30,280
Then it means Daeyoung will bid on it for sure.

487
00:29:30,450 --> 00:29:33,580
Our Secretary's Office obtains Intel before the NSP does.

488
00:29:33,750 --> 00:29:35,820
Right, Daeyoung makes cars, heavy equipment,

489
00:29:35,820 --> 00:29:37,650
and even ships.

490
00:29:37,650 --> 00:29:39,720
No wonder they want to buy a steel-producing company.

491
00:29:40,490 --> 00:29:42,830
To beat Daeyoung,

492
00:29:43,660 --> 00:29:46,730
we'd need at least 400 million dollars. Don't you think?

493
00:29:46,730 --> 00:29:48,830
It's not even a lucrative deal.

494
00:29:49,800 --> 00:29:53,540
Then should we forget about Hando Steel altogether?

495
00:29:53,540 --> 00:29:55,940
I will not let Daeyoung acquire Hando Steel.

496
00:29:57,740 --> 00:29:59,980
And the maximum amount we'll spend on this is 300 million.

497
00:30:01,010 --> 00:30:03,310
We won't spend a penny more.

498
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,250
Then how...

499
00:30:08,550 --> 00:30:10,020
Why are you asking me?

500
00:30:12,790 --> 00:30:14,060
- Vice-Chairman. - Yes, sir.

501
00:30:15,030 --> 00:30:18,800
Go make sure we can acquire Hando Steel.

502
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:19,900
Pardon?

503
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:23,170
Why? Are you not confident?

504
00:30:24,170 --> 00:30:26,000
Then step down. Why are you sitting here?

505
00:30:31,370 --> 00:30:32,410
What will you do?

506
00:30:34,810 --> 00:30:38,550
My goodness. Thanks. This looks delicious.

507
00:30:39,580 --> 00:30:43,190
Do Jun, you're such a perfect grandson.

508
00:30:43,220 --> 00:30:44,990
You came all the way here...

509
00:30:44,990 --> 00:30:48,290
to see your grandparents after your trip to the US.

510
00:30:48,790 --> 00:30:50,790
Just like your father, you're handsome,

511
00:30:50,790 --> 00:30:53,500
smart, and sweet.

512
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:55,730
Right, Jeong Rae?

513
00:30:56,300 --> 00:30:58,870
I'd say he got his looks from his mother.

514
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:02,240
As for his brain... I don't know.

515
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:08,280
Use your smart brain to follow in your grandpa's footsteps...

516
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:11,210
and grow the company.

517
00:31:12,350 --> 00:31:13,880
Why not study management?

518
00:31:13,880 --> 00:31:17,250
Why would you suddenly want to go to law school?

519
00:31:18,390 --> 00:31:20,390
He takes after his father,

520
00:31:20,390 --> 00:31:24,660
so I guess he has no interest in running a business whatsoever.

521
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:26,130
Right, Do Jun?

522
00:31:28,430 --> 00:31:29,800
If I study law,

523
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:32,900
I can be more helpful to Grandpa and his business.

524
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:34,700
Really?

525
00:31:35,070 --> 00:31:38,880
My gosh. Is that why you decided to study law, Do Jun?

526
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:42,850
Grandma, I'm still in my first year.

527
00:31:44,780 --> 00:31:48,250
At the moment, I just want to play and not think about anything.

528
00:31:48,950 --> 00:31:51,220
Yes! Just play.

529
00:31:51,220 --> 00:31:53,360
That's what you should do when you're in your first year.

530
00:31:53,690 --> 00:31:55,160
Meet some girls too, okay?

531
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:56,390
The board meeting is over.

532
00:31:56,390 --> 00:31:58,190
I see. You can go upstairs now, Do Jun.

533
00:31:58,190 --> 00:31:59,230
Okay, Grandma.

534
00:31:59,660 --> 00:32:01,630
- Thank you. - Just play!

535
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,300
Goodness, that old man is awfully stubborn.

536
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:09,870
Acquire Hando Steel, but don't spend money.

537
00:32:09,870 --> 00:32:13,040
What are we supposed to do, then?

538
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:17,750
Right, Young Ki?

539
00:32:27,020 --> 00:32:28,760
Do Jun, you're back!

540
00:32:31,330 --> 00:32:33,230
You little rascal.

541
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:37,000
Did you see lots of cool things in the US?

542
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,200
- Did you eat lots of good food? - Yes, Grandpa.

543
00:32:39,740 --> 00:32:41,000
Thanks to you...

544
00:32:42,170 --> 00:32:43,340
I had a great trip.

545
00:32:43,470 --> 00:32:44,510
Good.

546
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:47,040
What was your favourite out of all the dishes you tried there?

547
00:32:48,610 --> 00:32:52,020
- Pardon me? - What was your favourite dish?

548
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:54,520
Oh.

549
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:01,020
The donut.

550
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:10,100
That brat.

551
00:33:12,170 --> 00:33:14,600
Does he think he's Lee Mi Ja or Cho Yong Pil...

552
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:16,410
who just returned from his concert tour in Southeast Asia?

553
00:33:16,640 --> 00:33:17,640
Goodness.

554
00:33:19,910 --> 00:33:21,010
I'm talking about Do Jun.

555
00:33:21,540 --> 00:33:23,880
He was in New York for a few days with his dad.

556
00:33:24,010 --> 00:33:27,280
And he showed up to report to Father that he's back.

557
00:33:27,780 --> 00:33:30,420
Hey. He's just 20, and he's a guy.

558
00:33:30,420 --> 00:33:32,220
Guys his age are rarely that attentive.

559
00:33:33,260 --> 00:33:35,430
I bet he has an ulterior motive.

560
00:33:36,230 --> 00:33:39,900
At age 20, he should know how to respect his elders.

561
00:33:40,230 --> 00:33:41,430
He's better than his dad.

562
00:33:43,870 --> 00:33:46,900
You're so understanding.

563
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:49,040
You're incredibly magnanimous.

564
00:33:49,340 --> 00:33:50,340
But you see,

565
00:33:51,540 --> 00:33:52,610
did you know that Do Jun...

566
00:33:53,210 --> 00:33:55,210
exchanged the 24 billion won to US dollars before his trip?

567
00:33:55,210 --> 00:33:57,210
The price of our father's life?

568
00:33:58,850 --> 00:34:00,880
It wouldn't have been possible without Father's permission.

569
00:34:04,390 --> 00:34:06,460
He's different from his dad.

570
00:34:07,060 --> 00:34:09,660
Yoon Ki never had any interest in the company.

571
00:34:09,660 --> 00:34:12,030
But that boy is different. Just look at his eyes.

572
00:34:13,100 --> 00:34:17,170
We have to stay frosty, Young Ki.

573
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:23,240
That it's allowance? That it's a simple gift?

574
00:34:25,840 --> 00:34:27,310
It could be a test.

575
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:30,750
Go make sure we can acquire Hando Steel.

576
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:35,220
Father could be testing the boy with plans on picking a successor.

577
00:34:36,220 --> 00:34:38,820
Why? Are you not confident?

578
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:41,690
Then step down. Why are you sitting here?

579
00:34:48,470 --> 00:34:50,070
(Jin Young Ki)

580
00:34:50,070 --> 00:34:52,040
I told the Economic Research Institute...

581
00:34:52,040 --> 00:34:54,870
to prepare a report to send to Hando Steel's creditors.

582
00:34:55,640 --> 00:34:58,610
If we emphasize the number of jobs that will be created...

583
00:34:58,610 --> 00:35:00,680
when we acquire Hando Steel and the positive synergy,

584
00:35:01,340 --> 00:35:03,180
Cheongwadae will show interest too.

585
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:06,850
Risk management is crucial as the administration is nearing its end.

586
00:35:09,490 --> 00:35:11,590
Please proceed accordingly, Mr. Lee.

587
00:35:14,390 --> 00:35:15,460
Yes, sir.

588
00:35:22,230 --> 00:35:23,230
Hang Jae.

589
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:35,510
My old man...

590
00:35:37,950 --> 00:35:39,680
What does he want from me?

591
00:35:41,020 --> 00:35:42,950
Acquiring Hando Steel?

592
00:35:43,890 --> 00:35:44,920
Or...

593
00:35:46,860 --> 00:35:48,590
is he just not happy with anything I do?

594
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:54,130
You know what he's thinking better than his own children do.

595
00:35:56,530 --> 00:35:57,600
Mr. Chairman...

596
00:35:58,940 --> 00:36:03,010
would like to pass Soonyang down to someone who is like him.

597
00:36:03,770 --> 00:36:05,240
And it might not be his eldest son?

598
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:07,910
Young Ki, he is giving you a chance first...

599
00:36:07,910 --> 00:36:09,050
because you're his eldest son.

600
00:36:14,420 --> 00:36:17,050
Focus on acquiring Hando Steel.

601
00:36:18,250 --> 00:36:22,030
He wants to see the fighting spirit and persistence in you.

602
00:36:24,630 --> 00:36:26,460
To him, running a company...

603
00:36:27,230 --> 00:36:29,730
was like a never-ending war,

604
00:36:30,700 --> 00:36:32,540
where he had to kill first in order to survive.

605
00:36:39,010 --> 00:36:40,010
Sir.

606
00:36:41,110 --> 00:36:43,250
As you had predicted, Vice-Chairman Jin...

607
00:36:43,250 --> 00:36:45,380
asked me what you were really thinking.

608
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:52,260
I told him that you were giving him a chance...

609
00:36:52,990 --> 00:36:55,090
and that nothing would change...

610
00:36:55,560 --> 00:36:58,190
if he did his best to acquire Hando Steel.

611
00:36:58,860 --> 00:36:59,900
I assured him.

612
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:04,930
Hang Jae.

613
00:37:06,370 --> 00:37:08,740
It's such a shame.

614
00:37:09,740 --> 00:37:10,740
Pardon me?

615
00:37:11,170 --> 00:37:14,540
Why were you born to your parents?

616
00:37:17,110 --> 00:37:19,350
I wish you were my son.

617
00:37:24,690 --> 00:37:25,960
Sir, didn't you know?

618
00:37:26,660 --> 00:37:30,390
I think of you as my father.

619
00:37:35,130 --> 00:37:36,170
I'll leave you to it.

620
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,640
You see, Do Jun...

621
00:37:45,140 --> 00:37:47,780
His school is pretty far from where he lives.

622
00:37:50,310 --> 00:37:52,450
Send him a car.

623
00:37:53,050 --> 00:37:54,050
Yes, sir.

624
00:38:05,030 --> 00:38:07,330
Hello, I'm Ha In Seok from the Secretary's Office.

625
00:38:07,930 --> 00:38:09,100
Hello.

626
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:10,830
Mr. Chairman sent me.

627
00:38:11,030 --> 00:38:12,340
He said your school was pretty far,

628
00:38:12,340 --> 00:38:13,640
so it must be hard for you to commute.

629
00:38:18,640 --> 00:38:20,240
I'll be your driver from now on.

630
00:38:37,090 --> 00:38:38,900
Please just drop me off in front of the gate.

631
00:38:39,260 --> 00:38:40,700
I'll walk from there.

632
00:38:41,030 --> 00:38:43,300
No, I'll drop you off in front of the lecture hall.

633
00:38:43,870 --> 00:38:46,670
Most people at school already know who I am.

634
00:38:48,040 --> 00:38:51,340
I don't want to show up with a driver and attract attention.

635
00:38:52,510 --> 00:38:54,180
It won't do Grandpa any good.

636
00:38:55,280 --> 00:38:57,280
Right, I'll remember that.

637
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:03,420
(Seoul National University)

638
00:39:22,410 --> 00:39:25,070
I got it. I don't want to turn into a spoiled brat.

639
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:27,780
Oh, right.

640
00:39:28,280 --> 00:39:30,180
You're done for the day.

641
00:39:30,780 --> 00:39:34,220
You're free to decide how to spend the rest of your day.

642
00:39:34,450 --> 00:39:35,450
Bye.

643
00:39:40,060 --> 00:39:41,960
- Hello! - Come and take one!

644
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:45,760
- Take a look at this. - Please join us!

645
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:47,830
- Come find us! - Join us!

646
00:39:47,830 --> 00:39:49,930
- Hello, take one! - Welcome!

647
00:39:50,030 --> 00:39:51,630
- Hello, welcome! - Are you a freshman?

648
00:39:51,630 --> 00:39:52,900
- Would you be interested? - Hi.

649
00:39:52,900 --> 00:39:54,670
Come find us!

650
00:39:54,870 --> 00:39:56,370
You should join us.

651
00:40:07,850 --> 00:40:09,790
Jin Do Jun, at the School of Law. Right?

652
00:40:15,590 --> 00:40:16,960
I study law too. I'm Kim Tae Young.

653
00:40:17,260 --> 00:40:19,260
He's Gang Nam from the Department of Journalism.

654
00:40:19,260 --> 00:40:22,500
Come on, why is the introduction so bland? It's between us.

655
00:40:25,670 --> 00:40:27,470
Tae Young's family owns Mirae Industry.

656
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:29,370
My family owns Bando Firm.

657
00:40:29,740 --> 00:40:32,010
Ji Min's grandfather has been the Prime Minister since...

658
00:40:32,010 --> 00:40:33,080
So?

659
00:40:35,850 --> 00:40:39,650
Seong Jun must not have told you about our club, Prestigious Club.

660
00:40:40,450 --> 00:40:43,020
I did hear about it. Prestigious Club.

661
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:45,150
You used to call me casually, but now you treat me as your senior.

662
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:49,230
It was the center of Vice-Chairman Jin Seong Jun's connection.

663
00:40:49,590 --> 00:40:50,760
A secretive social gathering...

664
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:51,960
of the children of prestigious families.

665
00:40:52,090 --> 00:40:54,960
You don't have to act so stiff. It's nothing much.

666
00:40:55,670 --> 00:40:59,200
We're just inviting you to have a meal with those of your class.

667
00:41:00,200 --> 00:41:01,640
People are so strange.

668
00:41:02,140 --> 00:41:05,640
They feel a sense of incongruity because of people like us.

669
00:41:06,110 --> 00:41:08,480
So what? Is that our fault?

670
00:41:08,980 --> 00:41:10,480
It's their inferior complex.

671
00:41:10,710 --> 00:41:11,780
Yes.

672
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:14,580
What do you think, newbie?

673
00:41:14,580 --> 00:41:16,420
Enough with all the talking.

674
00:41:17,450 --> 00:41:18,490
Your number.

675
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:22,690
Why? Do I need your grandfather's permission to get your number?

676
00:41:24,090 --> 00:41:26,500
I'll text you the location and time of your welcoming dinner.

677
00:41:26,500 --> 00:41:29,770
You know it's a must to bring a partner, right?

678
00:41:40,280 --> 00:41:41,740
I must stick to the rule, right?

679
00:41:46,920 --> 00:41:48,680
Nice!

680
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:52,720
(Music Listening Room)

681
00:43:24,210 --> 00:43:25,480
We've met before, right?

682
00:43:31,290 --> 00:43:33,820
You look familiar. I definitely met you before.

683
00:43:34,560 --> 00:43:35,890
Where did we meet?

684
00:43:36,960 --> 00:43:38,930
You definitely have a classical taste.

685
00:43:40,900 --> 00:43:42,900
You could just invite me for a meal.

686
00:43:44,400 --> 00:43:46,600
Isn't this tactic way too classic?

687
00:43:49,570 --> 00:43:51,840
Hello, I'm not hitting on you.

688
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:53,810
Invite you for a meal?

689
00:43:54,080 --> 00:43:55,650
- When did I... - Here it is.

690
00:44:00,220 --> 00:44:01,480
This is what you're looking for, right?

691
00:44:17,800 --> 00:44:18,900
Let's have a meal.

692
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:47,830
("'Hello, I'm Jin Do Jun,' An Interview With Jin Do Jun...")

693
00:44:47,830 --> 00:44:49,300
("Who Entered Department of Law At the Top of His Class")

694
00:44:50,530 --> 00:44:51,830
There was a reason.

695
00:44:53,540 --> 00:44:56,410
Are you so confident and rude...

696
00:44:57,010 --> 00:44:58,610
because of your grandfather?

697
00:44:58,840 --> 00:45:00,310
No way.

698
00:45:01,310 --> 00:45:03,380
What's so hard about having a meal...

699
00:45:03,380 --> 00:45:05,780
with a peer in my department?

700
00:45:07,350 --> 00:45:10,590
Do I have to use my grandfather's power to eat with you?

701
00:45:14,260 --> 00:45:15,730
If you treat me to a nice meal,

702
00:45:16,590 --> 00:45:18,030
I was going to tell you...

703
00:45:18,030 --> 00:45:19,430
when Seo Tai Ji was making a comeback.

704
00:45:19,630 --> 00:45:20,800
I thought you might be curious.

705
00:45:22,200 --> 00:45:24,200
Is it fun to tease people?

706
00:45:29,970 --> 00:45:31,010
It's true, right?

707
00:45:32,610 --> 00:45:35,780
You said Soonyang's better than the CIA in getting information.

708
00:45:35,780 --> 00:45:37,780
That's how you heard it, right?

709
00:45:38,610 --> 00:45:41,720
I knew it. Is he really making a comeback?

710
00:45:42,650 --> 00:45:43,690
When?

711
00:45:46,520 --> 00:45:49,290
You're going to eat with me, right?

712
00:46:10,080 --> 00:46:12,850
She's there. Please stop here.

713
00:46:13,050 --> 00:46:14,080
Okay.

714
00:46:44,210 --> 00:46:46,980
Do you normally always wear like this?

715
00:46:53,990 --> 00:46:56,330
You're a bit different from the Seo Min Yeong I know.

716
00:46:57,230 --> 00:46:59,530
This? You're wrong.

717
00:47:00,330 --> 00:47:02,400
You must be thinking...

718
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:05,530
that I dolled up to meet you, but...

719
00:47:05,530 --> 00:47:08,300
You look better now. They're nice clothes.

720
00:47:17,050 --> 00:47:19,010
Tell me now. Is it true?

721
00:47:19,480 --> 00:47:20,720
Is he really making a comeback?

722
00:47:21,180 --> 00:47:22,280
Seo Tai Ji, I mean.

723
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:24,350
When is he coming back?

724
00:47:27,320 --> 00:47:28,420
You...

725
00:47:29,730 --> 00:47:31,560
Do you really know?

726
00:47:33,230 --> 00:47:35,300
After 4 years. The summer of 2000.

727
00:47:36,370 --> 00:47:38,830
He's coming back to celebrate the millennium, right?

728
00:47:39,540 --> 00:47:40,640
Not as a group.

729
00:47:41,170 --> 00:47:43,570
Seo Tai Ji continues as a soloist.

730
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:54,620
What's wrong?

731
00:47:56,020 --> 00:47:57,150
Are you disappointed?

732
00:47:58,250 --> 00:47:59,360
That's...

733
00:48:00,520 --> 00:48:01,890
just like Seo Tai Ji.

734
00:48:03,230 --> 00:48:04,960
You need new music for the new millennium.

735
00:48:08,260 --> 00:48:11,800
I kept my word. Can we go eat now?

736
00:48:12,030 --> 00:48:14,200
- Sure. - Okay. Let's go.

737
00:48:15,340 --> 00:48:18,140
- Seriously... - Go.

738
00:48:18,140 --> 00:48:20,210
- Hurry up. - Nice.

739
00:48:25,880 --> 00:48:28,380
This is the last time, okay?

740
00:48:28,380 --> 00:48:30,820
One more time.

741
00:48:35,460 --> 00:48:36,690
Order.

742
00:48:38,130 --> 00:48:39,760
Okay.

743
00:48:47,140 --> 00:48:49,340
You're here, Jin Do Jun.

744
00:48:50,670 --> 00:48:51,940
Gosh.

745
00:48:52,740 --> 00:48:55,680
It's really nice to see you in Prestigious Club.

746
00:48:58,210 --> 00:48:59,450
It's so nice to see you.

747
00:48:59,620 --> 00:49:00,820
We made a bet.

748
00:49:01,180 --> 00:49:02,890
Seong Jun said...

749
00:49:03,050 --> 00:49:04,850
you were a boring bookworm,

750
00:49:04,850 --> 00:49:07,320
so you would never join our club.

751
00:49:07,890 --> 00:49:09,020
Prestigious Club?

752
00:49:09,020 --> 00:49:10,930
She's Seo Min Yeong, also a freshman...

753
00:49:10,930 --> 00:49:13,060
of the Department of Law.

754
00:49:13,300 --> 00:49:14,360
Hold on.

755
00:49:21,270 --> 00:49:22,570
You're obedient.

756
00:49:23,040 --> 00:49:24,770
You only did this.

757
00:49:30,180 --> 00:49:31,450
She's a guest difficult to invite.

758
00:49:31,450 --> 00:49:32,720
Seo Min Yeong from Hanil Girls' High School.

759
00:49:33,350 --> 00:49:35,180
Her father is working in Seoul District Public Prosecutors' Office.

760
00:49:36,320 --> 00:49:38,450
In the end, you're here.

761
00:49:39,020 --> 00:49:40,220
As Do Jun's partner.

762
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:44,190
Anyway, welcome.

763
00:50:02,380 --> 00:50:04,750
This is Ha In Seok. Jin Do Jun,

764
00:50:04,980 --> 00:50:06,650
I mean, this is the route of 4-2.

765
00:50:15,020 --> 00:50:16,960
You should have told me the truth from the beginning.

766
00:50:17,690 --> 00:50:19,160
If I had known, I wouldn't have come.

767
00:50:20,500 --> 00:50:21,960
Why did you bring me here?

768
00:50:23,070 --> 00:50:25,330
- Because you're qualified. - What?

769
00:50:25,500 --> 00:50:27,170
Seo Min Yeong, the only child of Seo Yoon Ho,

770
00:50:27,340 --> 00:50:29,000
the deputy prosecutor...

771
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:30,670
of Seoul District Public Prosecutors' Office Special Unit.

772
00:50:32,610 --> 00:50:34,180
It's a social gathering that suits you.

773
00:50:34,180 --> 00:50:35,340
This Prestigious Club.

774
00:50:38,980 --> 00:50:40,150
It's a social gathering?

775
00:50:42,280 --> 00:50:45,190
Friendship where you back each other up when you're in trouble...

776
00:50:45,350 --> 00:50:48,360
once you each hold a position after graduating?

777
00:50:49,490 --> 00:50:52,860
Close-knit friendship...

778
00:50:53,030 --> 00:50:56,270
that ignores law and policies as if they're nothing?

779
00:50:57,330 --> 00:50:58,700
A social gathering, you said?

780
00:50:59,030 --> 00:51:00,740
Not a gathering of potential criminals?

781
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:05,170
Don't be mistaken, Jin Do Jun.

782
00:51:05,240 --> 00:51:08,480
What you can share here isn't deep friendship.

783
00:51:09,310 --> 00:51:11,180
It's a strong privilege.

784
00:51:11,650 --> 00:51:13,050
It doesn't suit me.

785
00:51:13,680 --> 00:51:16,350
I never had such a privilege...

786
00:51:16,620 --> 00:51:18,390
nor did I expect one.

787
00:51:22,620 --> 00:51:24,830
You're the one who's mistaken, Seo Min Yeong.

788
00:51:26,600 --> 00:51:30,300
So you think you're free from those privileges?

789
00:51:32,070 --> 00:51:35,200
Because you entered the best university in Korea...

790
00:51:35,200 --> 00:51:38,270
with the exam scores you worked hard to achieve with your smart brain.

791
00:51:42,710 --> 00:51:45,410
The fact that you were able to focus solely on studying...

792
00:51:45,410 --> 00:51:47,550
throughout the three years of high school.

793
00:51:48,620 --> 00:51:49,720
And the fact that you can only focus...

794
00:51:50,290 --> 00:51:52,690
on studying instead of worrying about making a living now.

795
00:51:53,760 --> 00:51:55,120
Haven't you thought...

796
00:51:55,120 --> 00:51:57,690
that it's thanks to your parents' financial and mental support?

797
00:52:00,830 --> 00:52:03,530
The family of bench and bar for generations.

798
00:52:03,530 --> 00:52:05,200
A healthy body and a smart brain.

799
00:52:06,100 --> 00:52:07,100
Have you never thought...

800
00:52:09,670 --> 00:52:12,740
that all of those were privileges given to you for free...

801
00:52:14,940 --> 00:52:16,480
ever since you were born?

802
00:52:32,760 --> 00:52:34,760
About Do Jun, sir.

803
00:52:35,830 --> 00:52:37,530
He's adjusting well to his university life...

804
00:52:37,530 --> 00:52:39,200
just like his peers.

805
00:52:43,370 --> 00:52:45,770
- Is that so? - Now's the best time in life.

806
00:52:46,110 --> 00:52:47,840
Even though he has 24 million dollars,

807
00:52:47,840 --> 00:52:49,340
he's still young.

808
00:52:52,380 --> 00:52:54,850
I wonder what he's thinking.

809
00:52:55,980 --> 00:52:57,050
Oh, well.

810
00:52:58,190 --> 00:53:00,960
You don't even know what your own son is thinking.

811
00:53:02,820 --> 00:53:04,130
He is...

812
00:53:05,990 --> 00:53:08,000
too distant of a family for me to know about him.

813
00:53:08,260 --> 00:53:12,600
Hando Steel reported bankruptcy as they could not manage the debt...

814
00:53:12,600 --> 00:53:14,670
from debt financing.

815
00:53:14,870 --> 00:53:18,070
Hando Steel has a debt over four billion dollars in total.

816
00:53:18,240 --> 00:53:22,510
Big social and economical impacts are expected.

817
00:53:22,640 --> 00:53:24,310
The company that placed 1th in wealth ranking.

818
00:53:24,310 --> 00:53:28,150
The company with the biggest debt of 4.2 billion dollars...

819
00:53:28,150 --> 00:53:29,990
collapsed in vain.

820
00:53:30,520 --> 00:53:32,590
Vice-Chairman Jin will attend the meeting...

821
00:53:32,590 --> 00:53:34,660
with the creditors himself.

822
00:53:38,430 --> 00:53:39,430
(Vice-Chairman's Office)

823
00:53:43,970 --> 00:53:45,500
We have a problem, sir.

824
00:53:46,030 --> 00:53:48,040
With the acquisition fund of 300 million dollars we prepared,

825
00:53:48,040 --> 00:53:50,040
we might not be able to negotiate.

826
00:53:50,410 --> 00:53:52,110
What are you saying now?

827
00:53:52,110 --> 00:53:55,040
There's a company that offered 500 million dollars...

828
00:53:55,480 --> 00:53:58,150
that the creditors demanded as the acquisition fund.

829
00:53:58,210 --> 00:53:59,680
Is it Daeyoung?

830
00:53:59,750 --> 00:54:00,780
Actually...

831
00:54:01,680 --> 00:54:03,350
It's a foreign investment company.

832
00:54:06,360 --> 00:54:08,690
Is there a special reason why a foreign company...

833
00:54:08,690 --> 00:54:09,760
took over a big Korean company?

834
00:54:09,760 --> 00:54:11,490
Are you going to take over Hando Steel?

835
00:54:11,490 --> 00:54:13,460
Did you really offer 500 million dollars?

836
00:54:13,460 --> 00:54:15,760
- Are you going to take over? - Please tell us!

837
00:54:15,760 --> 00:54:17,030
- Why did you do it? - Did you take over the company...

838
00:54:17,030 --> 00:54:18,270
at 500 million dollars?

839
00:54:18,270 --> 00:54:19,270
Of course.

840
00:54:19,840 --> 00:54:21,470
Power Shares is an investment company...

841
00:54:21,470 --> 00:54:23,110
that focuses on the future value.

842
00:54:23,710 --> 00:54:27,080
The 500 million dollars we offered is the future value of Hando Steel.

843
00:54:29,010 --> 00:54:31,110
An American investment company, Power Shares.

844
00:54:31,410 --> 00:54:33,780
Oh Se Hyeon, the representative of East Asia region.

845
00:54:33,780 --> 00:54:34,880
(Detailed Profile)

846
00:54:35,120 --> 00:54:36,620
He's an investment manager...

847
00:54:36,620 --> 00:54:38,120
who invests in companies' future values.

848
00:54:38,290 --> 00:54:41,190
He's a Korean-American who performs exceptionally well...

849
00:54:41,190 --> 00:54:42,560
when it comes to company takeovers.

850
00:54:43,330 --> 00:54:44,390
Future values?

851
00:54:45,090 --> 00:54:47,030
Why would a foreign investment company...

852
00:54:47,460 --> 00:54:48,960
that performed exceptionally well...

853
00:54:49,870 --> 00:54:50,930
want to take over...

854
00:54:51,470 --> 00:54:55,400
a weak and small company like Hando Steel?

855
00:54:56,240 --> 00:54:57,670
Just why?

856
00:55:04,750 --> 00:55:08,280
It's a chess piece.

857
00:55:10,590 --> 00:55:13,520
There must be the chess board's owner.

858
00:55:14,960 --> 00:55:16,760
The owner?

859
00:55:18,960 --> 00:55:20,460
Whoever...

860
00:55:21,630 --> 00:55:25,500
can't stand to watch Soonyang take over Hando Steel.

861
00:55:29,340 --> 00:55:30,610
That person is...

862
00:55:33,880 --> 00:55:35,580
the owner of the chess board.

863
00:55:44,690 --> 00:55:47,020
(Three Way Restaurant)

864
00:55:51,330 --> 00:55:53,800
(Three Way Restaurant)

865
00:55:54,000 --> 00:55:56,160
- Gosh! - My goodness.

866
00:55:56,160 --> 00:55:59,740
Gosh, Gyeong Hui. You said your back isn't well.

867
00:55:59,740 --> 00:56:01,400
Oh, dear.

868
00:56:01,840 --> 00:56:04,570
- You'll hurt your back. - It's okay.

869
00:56:04,570 --> 00:56:06,910
- Goodness. - I can't believe this.

870
00:56:07,240 --> 00:56:09,240
Gosh.

871
00:56:09,410 --> 00:56:11,380
- Be careful. - Okay.

872
00:56:11,510 --> 00:56:12,950
Goodness!

873
00:56:13,480 --> 00:56:15,750
You'll hurt yourself.

874
00:56:29,160 --> 00:56:30,470
Did you say he was Oh Se Hyeon?

875
00:56:31,030 --> 00:56:32,030
Yes.

876
00:56:33,370 --> 00:56:34,440
Dig into him.

877
00:56:36,570 --> 00:56:37,940
What he's thinking...

878
00:56:39,840 --> 00:56:41,040
and who he's meeting.

879
00:56:42,040 --> 00:56:43,040
Yes, sir.

880
00:57:09,300 --> 00:57:11,410
I shouldn't have gotten involved in the first place.

881
00:57:13,410 --> 00:57:16,240
Because of you, I am breaking my first rule...

882
00:57:16,650 --> 00:57:18,980
of investment for the first time.

883
00:57:21,650 --> 00:57:24,820
The corporate value of Hando Steel is 500 million dollars?

884
00:57:24,950 --> 00:57:25,950
No.

885
00:57:26,720 --> 00:57:29,190
Nevertheless, the investor wants to invest in it? Yes.

886
00:57:30,230 --> 00:57:31,230
Yes.

887
00:57:33,160 --> 00:57:34,400
Tell me the reason, at least.

888
00:57:35,630 --> 00:57:37,330
Why are you investing so recklessly?

889
00:57:39,130 --> 00:57:42,640
Keep investors' secrets no matter what happens.

890
00:57:44,610 --> 00:57:45,970
That's your investment rule, right?

891
00:57:51,450 --> 00:57:52,610
I have to stop Hando Steel...

892
00:57:53,680 --> 00:57:56,280
from falling into Vice-Chairman Jin's hands.

893
00:57:57,490 --> 00:57:58,490
Vice-Chairman Jin?

894
00:58:00,490 --> 00:58:03,460
He's your uncle. The successor of Soonyang.

895
00:58:04,530 --> 00:58:06,290
You should be nice to your family, so why...

896
00:58:09,500 --> 00:58:11,600
What you want...

897
00:58:13,340 --> 00:58:14,740
isn't just Hando Steel?

898
00:58:16,970 --> 00:58:18,510
In the end, what you want...

899
00:58:19,640 --> 00:58:20,680
is Soonyang?

900
00:58:24,680 --> 00:58:27,050
You want to become the owner of Soonyang?

901
00:58:38,560 --> 00:58:40,830
(Soonyang Group)

902
00:59:00,780 --> 00:59:04,850
(Reborn Rich)

903
00:59:35,450 --> 00:59:36,590
Are you asking because you don't know,

904
00:59:36,590 --> 00:59:37,720
or do you want to pretend that you don't know?

905
00:59:38,120 --> 00:59:39,120
It's my present.

906
00:59:39,190 --> 00:59:40,690
Do Jun.

907
00:59:40,690 --> 00:59:42,390
I prepared it to welcome you.

908
00:59:42,890 --> 00:59:43,890
Darn it.

909
00:59:43,890 --> 00:59:47,030
Don't give me another presumptuous advice.

910
00:59:47,130 --> 00:59:48,830
You're going to take over Hando Steel?

911
00:59:48,830 --> 00:59:51,170
You want to beat Daeyoung so bad.

912
00:59:51,230 --> 00:59:53,840
If you ever let Daeyoung take Hando Steel...

913
00:59:54,370 --> 00:59:58,070
The person who gave Daeyoung the money is someone from Soonyang.

914
00:59:58,470 --> 01:00:01,810
The eldest son succeeding. This isn't Joseon Dynasty.

915
01:00:02,210 --> 01:00:05,110
I'll show Father who I am.

916
01:00:05,750 --> 01:00:08,420
It's not over until it's over.

917
01:00:09,020 --> 01:00:11,420
I never forgave those...

918
01:00:12,290 --> 01:00:13,790
who went against me.

